<title>UK: Reed gains, continues recent uptrend.</title>
<headline>Reed gains, continues recent uptrend.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reed International Plc, the UK arm of publisher Reed Elsevier, gained 15 pence to 1,146-1/2 as it continued to rebound after a prolonged period of underperformance.</p>
<p>&quot;It has underperformed hugely against Elsevier,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>But dealers did not notice the arbitrage dealings which saw investors stepping out of Elsevier NV into Reed on Monday afternoon.</p>
<p>&quot;It seems more of a stock squeeze at the moment,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>Elsevier firmed 0.30 guilders to 31.40 in Amsterdam.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
